_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_

**Only persist the verification flag that actually changed.**

Line 293 now always writes `phoneVerification`, but several user-creation paths in this file never initialize that attribute. For email/magic-url logins this can turn the sparse update into `phoneVerification => null`, which risks validation failures or silently changing the stored shape.


<details>
<summary>💡 Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
     try {
-        $dbForProject->updateDocument('users', $user->getId(), new Document([
-            'emailVerification' => $user->getAttribute('emailVerification'),
-            'phoneVerification' => $user->getAttribute('phoneVerification'),
-        ]));
+        $updates = new Document();
+
+        if ($verifiedToken->getAttribute('type') === TOKEN_TYPE_MAGIC_URL || $verifiedToken->getAttribute('type') === TOKEN_TYPE_EMAIL) {
+            $updates->setAttribute('emailVerification', true);
+        }
+
+        if ($verifiedToken->getAttribute('type') === TOKEN_TYPE_PHONE) {
+            $updates->setAttribute('phoneVerification', true);
+        }
+
+        if (!$updates->isEmpty()) {
+            $dbForProject->updateDocument('users', $user->getId(), $updates);
+        }
     } catch (\Throwable $th) {
         throw new Exception(Exception::GENERAL_SERVER_ERROR, 'Failed saving user to DB');
     }
```
</details>

