_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟠 Major_

**Only include request-touched fields in this PATCH payload.**

This still writes both `name` and `subscribe` on every call, so a name-only update can overwrite a concurrent subscribe-only update with stale data. Build the sparse `Document` from the non-null request params instead of reading back from the mutated `$topic`.

<details>
<summary>♻️ Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-        $topic = $dbForProject->updateDocument('topics', $topicId, new Document([
-            'name' => $topic->getAttribute('name'),
-            'subscribe' => $topic->getAttribute('subscribe'),
-        ]));
+        $updates = [];
+
+        if (!\is_null($name)) {
+            $updates['name'] = $name;
+        }
+
+        if (!\is_null($subscribe)) {
+            $updates['subscribe'] = $subscribe;
+        }
+
+        if (!empty($updates)) {
+            $topic = $dbForProject->updateDocument('topics', $topicId, new Document($updates));
+        }
```
</details>

